sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Attendee
    participant Booker as Booker.tsx and useSchedule
    participant SlotsSvc as AvailableSlotsService (slots/util.ts)
    participant UASvc as UserAvailabilityService
    participant Slots as slots.ts
    participant ATS as AvailableTimeSlots
    participant AT as AvailableTimes
    participant OOO as OOOSlot
    participant Fmt as formatAwayWindow.ts
    participant Panel as OutOfOfficeInSlots

    Note over Attendee,Panel: Setup: a London host (BST, UTC+1) is away 2:00pm to 3:00pm for the doctor and 3:00pm to 4:00pm for travel on Oct 8, two entries that touch. In UTC that is 13:00Z to 14:00Z and 14:00Z to 15:00Z.

    Attendee->>Booker: open the booking page, pick Oct 8, zone and 12-hour format selected
    Booker->>SlotsSvc: trpc viewer.slots.getSchedule
    SlotsSvc->>UASvc: getUsersAvailability(users, query, initialData.outOfOfficeDays)
    Note over SlotsSvc,UASvc: Existing code from issue 104
    UASvc-->>SlotsSvc: datesOutOfOffice["2026-10-08"] = {entry data, windows: [doctor 13:00Z to 14:00Z, travel 14:00Z to 15:00Z]}

    SlotsSvc->>Slots: getSlots(dateRanges, eventLength, frequency, datesOutOfOffice, ...)
    loop for each slot start in buildSlotsWithDateRanges
        Slots->>Slots: findOutOfOfficeForSlot(dayData, windowsOfDay, slotStartMs, slotEndMs)
        Note over Slots: Modified type only. Returns the matching IOutOfOfficeWindow, or the whole-day record
        alt slot overlaps a window
            Slots->>Slots: slot {time, away, entry data, outOfOfficeStart: window.start, outOfOfficeEnd: window.end}
            Note over Slots: New. Copied only when the record has a start
        else whole-day record
            Slots->>Slots: slot {time, away, entry data}, no window fields
        else not away
            Slots->>Slots: slot {time}
        end
    end
    Slots-->>SlotsSvc: slots, 13:00Z marked away for the doctor and 14:00Z for travel
    SlotsSvc-->>Booker: slots grouped by date, with outOfOfficeStart and outOfOfficeEnd on away slots

    Booker->>ATS: render with scheduleData.slots
    ATS->>Fmt: dayPrintsNoTimes(slots)
    Note over ATS,Fmt: New. True only when every slot is away and none has outOfOfficeStart
    Fmt-->>ATS: false, so the header keeps the 12-hour and 24-hour toggle
    ATS->>AT: render the slots of Oct 8

    AT->>AT: oooAllDay = every slot inSamePanel(slots[0], slot)
    Note over AT: Modified. False here, because the day has bookable slots
    loop for each slot (merged with booked times)
        alt slot not away
            AT->>AT: SlotItem
        else previous slot is in the same panel (same window)
            AT->>AT: skip
        else first slot of a run with this window
            AT->>OOO: OOOSlot with this slot's entry data and window
            Note over AT,OOO: Modified. The window decides where a panel ends, so the doctor and travel entries give two panels
        end
    end

    loop for each OOOSlot (doctor, then travel)
        OOO->>OOO: useBookerTime() gives timezone and timeFormat, useLocale() gives i18n.language
        OOO->>Fmt: formatAwayWindow(outOfOfficeStart, outOfOfficeEnd, timezone, timeFormat, language)
        Note over OOO,Fmt: New. Day.js converts each instant to the booker's zone. A date is added to each time only when the two instants fall on different dates there
        Fmt-->>OOO: {start: "2:00pm", end: "3:00pm"} for a London attendee
        OOO->>Panel: render with awayWindow, notes, toUser
        Panel-->>Attendee: panel: emoji, "Host is OOO", "Away 2:00pm to 3:00pm", the public note, "Book Alex" redirect button
        Note over OOO,Panel: Modified. One new line under the is-OOO line, from the ooo_away_window string
    end

    opt attendee changes the time format or the zone
        Attendee->>Booker: toggle 12-hour or 24-hour, or pick another zone
        Booker->>OOO: re-render with the new useBookerTime values
        OOO->>Fmt: formatAwayWindow with the new zone or format
        Fmt-->>OOO: for example {start: "14:00", end: "15:00"}
        OOO->>Panel: render with the new awayWindow
        Panel-->>Attendee: "Away 14:00 to 15:00"
    end
